6	NHS-UEC-STD-006	UKHSA Cold Health Alert and Winter Surge Operational Escalation SOP	Severe Weather Escalation	UK Health Security Agency (UKHSA) Adverse Weather and Health Plan, AWHP-2024	The UKHSA Cold-Health Alert (CHA) system issues Yellow, Amber, and Red alerts based on Met Office temperature forecasts (sustained mean temperatures <= 2°C, severe frost days, and cold snap degree days). Under Amber and Red Cold Health Alerts, causal empirical evidence demonstrates a +2.058 percentage point breach rate increase in acute Type 1 emergency departments across the North West. Trusts must ramp up discharge lounges, establish daily morning system control calls with ICB partners, and ringfence acute frailty assessment units to mitigate cold-induced hypothermia, cardiovascular, and respiratory surges.	["Implement pre-discharge medication delivery to prevent discharge delays during severe sub-zero weather.", "Open supplementary surge capacity in accordance with pre-agreed Trust Winter Operational Plans.", "Ensure 100% staff flu and COVID-19 booster vaccination coverage and infection control protocols."]	[0.0010580466,0.0037591653,-0.015317121,0.024905734,-0.0114017315,0.023988279,0.00035994677,-0.014643364,-0.005192101,-0.04633942,-0.024102116,0.013550307,0.008674332,0.009060846,0.006751168,-0.010987727,0.018564552,-0.01809969,0.0015130573,-0.0038764118,0.017955432,-0.010365434,0.013290847,0.0046738307,-0.018245462,0.004199462,-0.007785017,-0.015781088,-0.015537411,0.12763703,-0.026774753,-0.016034923,0.004205647,-0.01034089,0.010982507,0.025896117,0.0071974755,-0.01158731,-0.0063324505,0.0118930815,-0.0035426887,-0.010836005,-0.0105265025,0.00024420812,0.00901591,-0.0020704332,-0.013174718,0.024642626,0.007766529,0.0034476877,-0.008847671,0.01613701,0.018898072,0.01919936,-0.0057790666,0.031945907,0.0062234798,0.022005416,-0.0013289388,0.02533642,0.0089940345,0.022180099,0.012266186,-0.0010682998,0.013981046,0.00017822348,0.03417121,0.026053544,1.5381262e-05,-0.0018298979,