1	NHS-UEC-STD-001	NHS England 4-Hour Emergency Access Standard (78% Operational Recovery Target)	Operational Access Standard	NHS England UEC Recovery Plan 2024-2026, Section 2.1	The NHS Constitutional standard mandates that at least 78% of patients attending Type 1 A&E must be admitted, transferred, or discharged within 4 hours of arrival. Acute trusts exceeding a 30% breach rate (performance below 70%) must trigger immediate clinical review of internal flow, activate acute medical assessment units, and engage local system partners for mutual aid. Liverpool University Hospitals NHS Foundation Trust (REM) operates as the regional benchmark anchor within Cheshire and Merseyside ICB (QE1) for 4-hour performance tracking.	["Activate rapid triage protocols within 15 minutes of patient arrival.", "Conduct senior decision-maker reviews for all patients with wait times exceeding 3 hours.", "Direct ambulant medical attendances to co-located Same Day Emergency Care (SDEC)."]	[0.0035712724,0.01219923,-0.010831306,0.0016581874,-0.024051785,0.011535756,-0.012239226,-0.025879996,-0.023713535,-0.033165373,-0.015454275,-0.0037274905,0.00052473595,0.01024583,0.0049788402,-0.010535789,0.009274511,-0.024410604,-0.027990047,0.0132354265,0.0056585562,-0.0023537276,0.013476649,-0.012674157,-0.028623158,0.003202283,-0.011420049,-0.014260867,-0.0098288,0.14286761,-0.023159645,-0.0075040213,-0.005300061,-0.0037719163,0.020133343,0.019800764,0.0051202048,-0.019239739,0.00336119,0.012288552,0.003326532,0.010613754,-0.0048342827,-0.0015961084,-0.009295797,-0.017621186,0.0024441439,0.013554892,-0.00078024436,-0.0060202503,0.008454312,0.007726737,0.01939851,-0.00050046487,0.03378802,0.024658814,0.009029266,0.014267955,0.017989468,0.00198532,-0.015573391,0.009024122,0.021721235,0.011129287,0.0004357905,0.01166126,0.04661726,-0.009036748,-0.0076399436,0.002100228,0.0032515654,-0.00089111336,-0.024926363,-0.014712105,0.017439347,-0.009437255,-0.024996636,-0.002530309,0.015620718,0.0093725985,-0.005