2	NHS-UEC-STD-002	45-Minute Maximum Ambulance Handover Protocol and Immediate Escalation	Ambulance Handover	NHS England Emergency Handover Guidance 2024/25, SOP-AMB-04	Ambulance handovers must be completed within 15 minutes of arrival, with an absolute upper ceiling of 45 minutes for complex handovers. Any handover exceeding 45 minutes constitutes an immediate clinical safety risk and patient harm hazard. The acute hospital leadership team (Executive on-call, Clinical Director, and Site Matron) must personally attend the Emergency Department to enact immediate offload protocols, initiate fit-to-sit cohorting, and facilitate rapid cohort nursing.	["Deploy Hospital Ambulance Liaison Officers (HALO) to expedite arrival-to-handover intervals.", "Establish designated cohort areas within ED footprint for patients awaiting inpatient bed transfer.", "Enact immediate clinical review when ambulance handover delays breach 45 minutes."]	[-0.014346953,0.014863516,0.00064742076,-0.013239881,-0.005578158,0.01353295,-0.02058187,-0.013858207,-0.018243369,-0.042505898,-0.01649439,0.010329931,0.006004053,0.029895496,0.023358375,-0.009716068,0.029945469,-0.026609965,-0.013373516,-0.0018741263,0.018875813,0.007826241,-0.0036318975,-0.0049830377,-0.0083018225,0.02366308,0.010206175,-0.007249548,-0.016002892,0.13435544,-0.038715042,0.00060190936,-0.019832876,-0.014469006,0.0038624022,0.006504278,0.0007310504,0.0032310782,-0.0041478854,0.018143777,0.006065473,-0.0037546481,-0.022563118,0.0033678715,0.011970184,-0.00073054776,0.0010281566,0.022167658,0.011404847,0.0120187905,-0.010371893,0.00662622,0.01870687,-0.010406513,0.013518928,0.009774884,0.013142613,0.015257506,0.027329968,0.019423688,-0.0032216113,0.006431251,-0.0049823658,0.0032360426,-0.018919589,-0.010845787,0.036959905,0.028724166,-0.012795182,0.024965115,0.028432176,0.008340915,-0.026210677,-0.0016546678,-0.0024976833,-0.02557868,-0.022413366,0.013646589,0.011695263,0.023056777,-0.009386603,0.000757652,-0.032716837,-0.00496935