3	NHS-UEC-STD-003	12-Hour Emergency Department Length of Stay Cap (<10% Wait Standard)	Length of Stay Standard	NHS England Quality and Patient Safety Standards, Section 4.3	Patients must not remain in an emergency department for longer than 12 hours from time of arrival. The national operational cap requires that less than 10% of total emergency admissions experience a stay greater than 12 hours. Prolonged stays correlate directly with inpatient mortality, hospital-acquired deconditioning, and nosocomial infection. Zero tolerance is enforced for corridor care and unallocated trolley waits lasting beyond 12 hours.	["Enact full-capacity protocol (FCP) transferring stable inpatients to ward corridors if ED capacity is exhausted.", "Notify ICB System Control Centre when 12-hour trolley waits exceed 5 concurrent cases.", "Coordinate immediate emergency discharges via Discharge to Assess (D2A) pathway 0."]	[-0.008541919,0.010285875,0.0028343233,-0.0004210904,-0.01782922,0.006596797,-0.007797692,0.010551697,-0.006202307,-0.03546776,-0.022939805,0.015824886,0.010066064,0.019623894,0.020893984,-0.022658303,0.0114474,-0.020623127,-0.01952695,0.026343646,-0.0024072612,0.0048749563,0.018577961,-0.0012578884,0.00061113376,0.0144013,-0.000313075,-0.00403761,-0.011326997,0.13936478,-0.0074064485,-0.005454354,-0.009949331,-0.014685983,0.0018385671,0.03960546,0.008534357,0.018242825,-0.018153682,-0.0040344144,-0.0024312837,0.006739791,-0.014122529,-0.010541472,0.0127919335,-0.011044914,-0.0041719475,0.018451577,0.009525482,0.0058115665,-0.001485596,0.007932998,0.01829332,-0.0035165425,0.010628494,0.009969036,-0.0035986654,0.029735755,0.026634568,-0.0014393792,-0.013276568,0.018771611,0.004308227,0.0042175045,-0.0077706287,-0.01139704,0.030494474,0.019183706,-0.009460988,0.00135038,0.021155491,0.030635668,-0.029498648,-0.015308137,0.00073598936,-0.029164245,-0.02471105,0.0014751975,0.01418613,0.027561087,-0.00727693,0.0025709833,-0.019940594,0.009372775,-0.009204633,-0.0005072142,-0.