7	NHS-UEC-STD-007	Operational Pressures Escalation Levels (OPEL 1-4) Regional Trigger Framework	Escalation Framework	NHS England OPEL National Framework and Operational Guidance 2024, OPEL-REF-01	The national OPEL framework classifies hospital pressure into four standardized tiers: OPEL 1: Normal operational capacity within planned resources. OPEL 2: Moderate pressure; Trust initiates internal bed and discharge reviews. OPEL 3: Severe pressure; acute breach rate >30%, bed occupancy >92%, ambulance handover delays emerging. OPEL 4: Critical operational emergency; Trust is unable to deliver comprehensive care and patient safety is compromised. Declaring OPEL 4 mandates immediate regional ICB escalation, cancellation of non-urgent elective surgical admissions, deployment of mutual aid across neighboring acute trusts, and opening of all surge beds.	["Convene Trust Executive Emergency Escalation Huddle within 60 minutes of OPEL 3 or 4 declaration.", "Notify ICB System Control Centre and regional ambulance dispatch service (NWAS).", "Enforce discharge-before-noon quotas across all adult acute inpatient wards."]	[0.0009478656,0.01349194,-0.006614825,0.005974518,-0.0026087984,0.012462856,-0.020497369,-0.0066069225,-0.002959994,-0.04541003,-0.017813204,0.0035003708,0.002739474,0.0021093155,0.006285661,0.0053935866,0.023819996,-0.0073196115,0.0023471962,0.004179937,0.021617291,0.008373086,0.0048558284,0.009421272,0.0001626304,0.0047817817,0.001334012,-0.0014253734,-0.012856958,0.14329745,-0.014236316,-0.0014675235,-0.0059602866,-0.00017550733,-0.0018956879,0.010050954,0.012922136,0.0074351085,-0.0018928362,-0.009420395,0.017134149,-0.024211194,-0.016647886,0.0042593437,-0.010446439,-0.0032404282,0.001174074,0.02113437,-0.0048392345,0.0065614455,0.009714653,0.010291704,0.019334609,0.005665458,0.012821034,0.016652795,-0.0019483216,0.013941183,0.023260914,0.0059279315,-0.011393142,-0.001095567,0.011351245,0.0025669532,-0.0029775186,-0.004105851,0.028699597,-0.00027552526,-0.0249