8	NHS-UEC-STD-008	Cheshire and Merseyside ICB Urgent Care Catchment Mutual Aid Protocol	Regional Mutual Aid	NHS Cheshire and Merseyside ICB Urgent Care Operational Policy, CM-ICB-2024-03	Cheshire and Merseyside ICB (QE1) oversees acute trusts including Liverpool University Hospitals NHS FT (REM), Countess of Chester Hospital (RJR), Wirral University Teaching Hospital (RBL), Warrington and Halton Hospitals (RWW), Alder Hey Children's NHS FT (RBS), and Liverpool Women's NHS FT (REP). When an acute trust within 25 km of Liverpool REM declares OPEL 4 or experiences severe ambulance handover delays, the ICB System Coordination Centre (SCC) can dynamically re-route 999 emergency ambulances to proximate peer trusts with available capacity and activate cross-system Single Point of Access (SPoA) diversion.	["Evaluate inverse-distance-weighted catchment spillover before requesting inter-trust transfers.", "Engage North West Ambulance Service (NWAS) for dynamic hospital diverts across the Mersey corridor.", "Conduct twice-daily cross-trust bed capacity teleconferences chaired by the ICB Medical Director."]	[-0.025362486,0.017309567,-0.022759855,0.011069701,-0.00820016,0.01613331,-0.012223338,-0.029926596,-0.03310225,-0.03756624,-0.0047512036,-0.010774492,0.015101459,0.005247643,0.014577347,-0.007055372,0.016657798,-0.022069732,-0.016215047,-0.010764874,0.016663348,-0.008908814,0.009420867,-0.014140549,-0.025193226,0.014110954,-0.008717237,-0.02240373,-0.012236796,0.13810752,-0.027857266,-0.0020825488,-0.018095052,-0.007618875,0.0013273037,0.014337394,0.009421599,-0.014221107,0.00094908295,0.004597789,0.015028029,0.0027286303,-0.01982252,0.0033456194,0.006924363,-0.022708684,0.008919916,0.0065393117,0.013718716,0.0066780765,-0.011136357,0.010770011,0.01727987,-0.0055363723,0.021526303,0.0185887,0.018726164,0.008003373,0.009514024,0.012256097,-0.0074128476,0.0024298853,0.01011485,0.020636236,0.0008471419,-0.003240162,0.024602843,0.013090904,-0.017223332,0.004222596,-0.005423381,